# Copy to .env.local, fill in, then rebuild. All values are public (inlined into the static site).
#
# Firebase setup, in this order. The web API key becomes public, so finish it before going live:
#  1. Firestore Database > Create database > keep the database ID "(default)" > choose a location (cannot be
#     changed later) > Start in PRODUCTION mode. Never test mode: it leaves every enquiry publicly readable.
#     Then run `firebase deploy --only firestore` (rules + TTL policies) before any build that writes to it goes live.
#  2. Project settings > General > Your apps: add a Web app and copy its apiKey into NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_API_KEY below.
#  3. Authentication > Sign-in method: enable Email/Password.
#  4. Immediately after: Authentication > Settings > User actions: untick "Enable create (sign-up)".
#  5. Only then: Authentication > Users > Add user support@brightonsolution.com (Add user in the console still works
#     with sign-up disabled). Sign in on /admin and send the verification email from there.
#     Never click a verification email you did not request from /admin yourself.
#  6. Firestore > TTL policies: check that pageviews.expireAt and events.expireAt are listed (deployed in step 1).
#  7. Google Cloud console > APIs & Services > Credentials > browser key: Application restrictions = HTTP referrers
#     brightonsolution.com/*, *.brightonsolution.com/*, brighton-web-ea63c.web.app/*, brighton-web-ea63c.firebaseapp.com/*;
#     API restrictions = Identity Toolkit API, Token Service API, Cloud Firestore API.
#  8. Billing > Budgets & alerts: a low monthly budget alert for the project.

# Web API key from Firebase console > Project settings > General > Your apps (required for /admin sign-in).
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
# Firebase project id (defaults to brighton-web-ea63c when empty).
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=brighton-web-ea63c
# Web app id from the same settings page (optional).
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_APP_ID=
# Google Analytics 4 measurement id (G-XXXXXXX); when set, visitors see a consent bar before GA loads.
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_MEASUREMENT_ID=
# Set to "true" to switch off first-party visitor analytics.
NEXT_PUBLIC_ANALYTICS_DISABLED=
# Set to "true" (or run npm run build:maintenance) to show the maintenance screen on every page.
NEXT_PUBLIC_MAINTENANCE_MODE=
